    "rfc_section": "RFC 9112 §6.1",
    "severity": "ambiguous",
    "notes": "Extra OWS before value is RFC-legal but after stripping the value is 'chunked' which matches. However strict mode checks the raw value before OWS stripping and finds ' chunked' (with leading space), which is caught by _strip_ows_bounds then compared exactly. Parser strips OWS then compares, so this actually passes strict. Reject rationale: defense-in-depth against TE obfuscation — but our parser correctly normalizes OWS.",
    "description": "Transfer-Encoding with extra leading space before 'chunked'",
    "input": {
      "wire_hex": "504f5354202f20485454502f312e310d0a486f73743a206578616d706c652e636f6d0d0a5472616e736665722d456e636f64696e673a20206368756e6b65640d0a0d0a300d0a0d0a"
    },
    "expected": {
      "behavior": "accept",
      "reason": "OWS is stripped before value comparison, resulting in exact 'chunked' match"
    }
  },
